.TH SDL_wcsstr 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_wcsstr \- Search a wide string for the first instance of a specific substring.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "wchar_t * SDL_wcsstr(const wchar_t *haystack, const wchar_t *needle);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The search ends once it finds the requested substring, or a null terminator byte to end the string\[char46]
.PP
Note that this looks for strings of _wide characters_, not _codepoints_, so it\(aqs legal to search for malformed and incomplete UTF-16 sequences\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I haystack
the wide string to search\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I needle
the wide string to search for\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the first instance of
.BR needle
in the string, or NULL if not found\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

